        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fe9261599d614784b62430af2f87ea4a",
      "statement": "The per-request route handler renames `path_params['proxy'] = path_params.pop('path')` only when `route.is_greedy and 'path' in path_params`, preserving `{path}` parameters on non-greedy routes; the synthesized Lambda event is built by `build_event()` outside the serialization lock using the request, path params, route's `resource_path`, event format, and auth context, and `normalize_response()` translates the handler result to an HTTP response after the lock is released, handling `None`, dicts with `statusCode` (including base64-decoded bodies and dict bodies JSON-encoded), dicts without `statusCode` (auto-wrapped as JSON 200), and string/primitive returns, while uncaught handler exceptions produce a 500 response with the traceback as plain text and structured logging at `[METHOD] /path -> FunctionName (statusCode, duration_ms)`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/easysam/local_server.py#L191-L237",
