    {
      "id": "claim_2e1e8dff04324c9a9c777abdaebcacaa",
      "statement": "Binary request bodies are base64-encoded when the content type is in `BINARY_CONTENT_TYPES` (`application/octet-stream`, `image/png`, `image/jpeg`, `image/gif`, `image/webp`, `application/pdf`, `application/zip`); otherwise the body is decoded as UTF-8 with error replacement, and `normalize_response` decodes base64-encoded response bodies when `isBase64Encoded: True`, using the `Content-Type` header for the media type or falling back to `application/octet-stream` for binary and `application/json` otherwise.",
