    {
      "id": "claim_053be8b60e514c4194c086f56cfc6f9a",
      "statement": "Authorizer Lambdas are not executed locally — instead `--auth-context` provides a fixed `requestContext.authorizer` payload injected into every request's event, parsed by `_parse_json_option` which tries a file path first (trapping `OSError`/`ValueError` on Windows for inline JSON strings) then falls back to inline JSON parsing, with the injection differing by format (v1 puts the dict directly under `requestContext.authorizer`; v2 wraps it under `requestContext.authorizer.lambda`); the implementation explicitly does not include hot reload, local timeout enforcement from `resources.yaml`, or per-route auth context selection, and allows infinite handler execution for debugging.",
      "evidence": [
