    {
      "id": "claim_f81ac97cf7a740f8b6f9f93d4d62bed4",
      "statement": "The local execution workflow differs from the cloud deployment path in how `common/` modules are resolved: during `deploy`, `commondep.py` AST-analyzes each lambda's imports and copies only the used `common/` modules into each lambda's directory, whereas in local mode the copy step is skipped and `sys.path` is set to `[lambda_dir, project_root]` so `import common.utils` resolves directly from source, relying on the selective `sys.modules` purge in `isolated_import_context` to pick up `common/` changes between requests; the default bind address is `127.0.0.1` (loopback only), CORS is wide-open for local development, and `--auth-context` is global across all routes.",
